sam: LuminaHealth POC hit a streaming issue in the iOS embedded webview during the executive demo. EventSource closes immediately and client throws 'Unexpected token < in JSON at position 0'. They pasted the first bytes from the stream: <html><body>502 Bad Gateway... then partial JSON after. Anyone seen HTML injector/edge error pages corrupting SSE frames?

priya: that usually means a proxy or edge returned an HTML error page mid-stream. request-id? SDK/version?

sam: request-id=lum-req-202604, using our iOS SDK 1.4.2 wrapped in WKWebView. Customer also tried raw EventSource in the app and saw same.

nate: can repro locally with a flaky upstream returning 502 during transfer. curl -N shows HTML page mixed with data: lines.

```
curl -N -H "Accept: text/event-stream" "https://stream.redwood.example/stream?req=lum-req-202604"
# response begins:
# data: {"id":"r1","choices":[{"text":"Starting\"}
# then later: <html>502 Bad Gateway</html>
```

olga: two things: 1) clients must be defensive (ignore non-JSON prefixes), 2) we should stop middleboxes from injecting error pages. Can eng-infra check upstream health and proxy error templates?

priya: also confirm our edge sets X-Accel-Buffering: no and sends chunked transfer encoding. Some CDNs rewrite error bodies into HTML which is the culprit. I'll pull the edge logs for lum-req-202604.

nate: quick client workaround: strip leading HTML if you detect '<' before '{', or only attempt JSON.parse if first non-whitespace char is '{' or '['. snippet:

```
let buf='';
source.onmessage = e => {
  buf += e.data;
  const head = buf.trimLeft().slice(0,1);
  if (head !== '{' && head !== '[') {
    // buffer might contain injected HTML or partial error page, drop until we see JSON start
    const idx = buf.indexOf('{');
    if (idx === -1) return;
    buf = buf.slice(idx);
  }
  try {
    const obj = JSON.parse(buf);
    handle(obj);
    buf = '';
  } catch(err) {
    // incomplete JSON, wait for more
  }
};
```

olga: we should also add a sentinel event at end of stream (e.g., data: [DONE]) so clients can be more robust. For POC we can enable sentinel on the service.

deploy-bot: deploy 2026-04-12T09:07:14 started to eng-runtime (rollout id r-20260412).

priya: infra found that a cache tier returned a 502 for this request and the HTML body was injected by the CDN edge. Eng-runtime, can you plumb through a no-transform or passthrough for SSE endpoints?

nate: also saw that rate-limited backends return HTML error pages for some 429s when under load. Are we exposing 429 bodies as JSON anywhere? If not, CDN fallback is replacing with HTML.

olga: action items: (1) sales send customer the defensive client snippet and ask them to retry, (2) eng-runtime to enable sentinel events + ensure SSE endpoints bypass CDN error rewriting, (3) infra to investigate the specific cache 502 for lum-req-202604.

sam: I'll send the snippet to LuminaHealth and schedule a short screenshare. thanks all. :pray:
